<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74837" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρει-τύπος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>working in the mountains</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρειτύποι,</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).49
			</span></i>, were <i>wood-cutters</i> and <i>quarry-men, who brought
				down materials from the mountains</i> :—so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεοτύποι</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.3.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.12.4
			</span></i>, al. (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρει-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CP</u>
					5.11.3
				</span></i>
			) ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀροιτύποι</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				377
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.445
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eleg.Alex.Adesp.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i> ; cf. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀροτύπος.</span></div>
